            "title": "Attachment Id"
          },
          "url": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "description": "The replacement link target, read ONLY when the pinned artifact's kind is 'link' - where it IS required, a blank one being a 400. It is CHECKED, but never fetched: it must begin with https:// or http:// (case-insensitive) and be at most 2048 characters (Unicode runes, not bytes), and anything else is a 400 - never a silent truncation. Unlike name and description, url has NO carry-forward branch here: replace re-validates it on EVERY call, so a caller that only means to rename the deliverable must send back a url that passes both checks. Past those two checks it is stored exactly as sent and still never fetched, so a typo replaces a working deliverable with one that leads nowhere. The two checks bind NEW writes only: stored urls predating them are left as they are. Sending it for a file/image artifact is refused rather than ignored, because such a request means the caller believes the kind can change.",
            "title": "Url"
